 35   c  ABST$This work presents a comprehensive and critical evaluation of     
 35  2c  experimental nuclear spectroscopic data from reactions and decays for  
 35  3c  all 11 known nuclides with mass number 35                              
 35  4c  (Ne,Na,Mg,Al,Si,P,S,Cl,Ar,K,Ca). Recommended values are produced for   
 35  5c  level energies, spins and parities, half-lives, and radiation          
 35  6c  properties including energies, branching ratios, and multipolarities of
 35  7c  |g rays, as well as characteristics of |b radiation decays, based on a 
 35  8c  rigorous assessment of all available experimental data. Discrepancies  
 35  9c  among existing results are carefully addressed. This work supersedes   
 35  Ac  earlier full evaluations of A=35 published by 2011Ch48, 1990En08 (also 
 35  Bc  1998En04 update) and 1978En02.                                         
 35   c  {+35}Cl remains the most extensively studied nuclide, investigated     
 35  2c  through 28 different reactions and decays, followed by {+35}S, {+35}P, 
 35  3c  and {+35}Ar. For {+35}Na, only two excited states have been observed,  
 35  4c  and its |b{+-}-decay scheme has not yet been established. For {+35}Mg, 
 35  5c  no |g rays have been placed with certainty, and no decay dataset exists
 35  6c  on {+35}Mg|){+35}Al. Many {+35}Ar levels of astrophysical interest were
 35  7c  identified in a high-resolution {+36}Ar(d,t){+35}Ar measurement, but   
 35  8c  without assignments of J, |p, C{+2}S, or lifetimes. Low-energy {+35}K          
 35  9c  %(|e+|b{++})-delayed protons remain unclear. For {+35}K, many excited  
 35  Ac  states discovered via {+35}Ca |e+|b{++} decay are unresolved. For      
 35  Bc  {+35}Ca, no |g rays have been observed and only one excited state has  
 35  Cc  been identified. Notably, {+35}Ca is the only nuclide in this mass     
 35  Dc  chain that decays by |e+|b{++}-delayed two protons, although the       
 35  Ec  emission mechanism remains unclear.                                    
 74   c  CUT$Literature available up to September 30, 2025 has been consulted,  
 74  2c  with the help of the primary bibliographic source, the NSR database    
 74  3c  (2014Pr09) available at Brookhaven National Laboratory web page: 74 #c 
 74  4c  www.nndc.bnl.gov/nsr/                                                  
 74   c  COMM$The statistical analysis of |g-ray data and deduced level schemes 
 74  2c  is carried out through a suite of current versions of computer codes   
 74  3c  available at the IAEA-NDS web page of ENSDF codes                      
 74  4c  (https://www-nds.iaea.org/public/ensdf_pgm) such as GLSC, Java-RULER,  
 74  5c  BrIccMixing, and ConsistencyCheck. The direct feedings to excited      
 74  6c  states in |b{+-} and |e decays have generally been computed from       
 74  7c  I(|g+ce) intensity balances at each level; the associated log {Ift}    
 74  8c  values are calculated using the BetaShape code. Theoretical total      
 74  9c  conversion coefficients are calculated using the version v2.3e of BrIcc
 74  Ac  code (2008Ki07) for frozen-orbit option with an implicit uncertainty of
 74  Bc  1.4% when not stated. Q values and particle separation energies have   
 74  Cc  been adopted from 2021Wa16 (AME2020). Static magnetic dipole moments   
 74  Dc  are taken from 2019StZV (long-lived states) and 2020StZV (short-lived  
 74  Ec  states) evaluations, and static electric quadrupole moments from       
 74  Fc  2021StZZ evaluation, when available in these publications. Nuclear rms 
 74  Gc  charge radii have been adopted from 2013An02 evaluation. In cases where
 74  Hc  weighted averaging procedures have been used, the assigned uncertainty 
 74  Ic  in the result is generally not lower than the lowest uncertainty in the
 74  Jc  data points used in the procedure.                                     
 35   c  ACKN$Earlier evaluations (2011Ch48, 1998En04 update, 1990En08,         
